@0    = ~Oh, welcome to my study. I am Master Shizell, the Seatower mage. You look like adventurers who get around. Amidst other things, I am on the lookout for a very rare black pearl. Not the usual kind, but one taken freshly from its shell. If you ever come across any, please consider bringing it here and I will compensate you accordingly.~
@1    = ~*hums*~
@2    = ~Hm... more powder or more liquid? It's all about the ratio!~
@3    = ~Slowly mixing... sloooowly... I don't want to repeat what happened last time.~
@4    = ~If stirred properly, this should be *just* as good as the expensive stuff!~
@5    = ~Just one more drop... That should do it.~
@6    = ~Is there anything else you want? We should focus on the doppelganger invasion now.~
@7    = ~I was told to come here if I want to fight against the doppelgangers.~
@8    = ~What exactly is this "mimic powder"? How does it work?~
@9    = ~Please show me your wares.~
@10   = ~Is there anything else you want?~
@11   = ~There is a fire elemental in the storeroom.~
@12   = ~Do you sell any magic items?~
@13   = ~The armorer made this umber hulk plate and said you had expressed interest in enchanting it?~
@14   = ~Please enchant the umber hulk plate.~
@15   = ~Where do you think I could find such a black pearl?~
@16   = ~Do you have any more errands for me?~
@17   = ~I have a black pearl here... would this suffice for your purposes?~
@18   = ~I found a fresh black pearl! It was in a sea cave right under this tower.~
@19   = ~I have a belladonna flower for you.~
@20   = ~I have a winter wolf pelt for you.~
@21   = ~I have an ankheg shell for you.~
@22   = ~We found some kind of ritual chamber down in the caves. Do you know anything about it?~
@23   = ~We cleared some kind of ritual chamber. It was a prison of a glabrezu.~
@24   = ~We cleared the ritual chamber. It was a prison of a glabrezu.~
@25   = ~I found some mimic blood. Do you have a use for it?~
@26   = ~Would you sell me back the mimic blood? I need it for something else.~
@27   = ~Do you have further use for the empty flask of your mimic "powder"?~
@28   = ~I'll be on my way.~
@29   = ~Yes, did he mention that? I have an idea for an enchantment. It would need one Potion of Clarity, one scroll of Armor, and one diamond. Oh, and I'd need payment, too: 6,000 gold. I should be able to make the armor suitable for killing more of its kind, by giving it protection against their strongest mind-affecting spells.~

@30   = ~With pleasure! I'm trying a new way of applying the enchantment, it's why I was interested in trying it on a freshly made hide armor. It should only take a moment!~
@31   = ~And—here you are! I think this worked quite well. I found potential to optimize a few things, though. I need to return to the drawing board, so please do not bring any more armor to me for the time being.~
@32   = ~I wasn't aware such a dungeon lies beneath the tower! This is fascinating. Hmm, I have a theory where it could originate from, but I'd need to do a lot of research to actually prove anything. Fact is, with all the history around Baldur's Gate in general and Balduran's Seatower especially, I am not surprised we find unknown dungeons beneath it.~
@33   = ~*Apparently*, there also is a sea cave that harbored a black pearl I wasn't aware of, either, for instance.~
@34   = ~A glabrezu is a mighty foe. It takes lots of magic to contain such a creature. Hmm, hmm, no, then my first theory about the origins of the dungeon does not hold. This will need much more investigation, yes, yes... Ah—thank you for informing me about this.~
@35   = ~The storeroom? How did it get there? Did the cook prod the fire too much? They do get attracted to great fires sometimes. Let the tower guard deal with it if you don't want to fight it yourself. Or, better yet, get it back into the fire. It needs to be big, though. A large fire will help it return to its home plane. I'm sure it didn't want to end up in a damp cellar.~
@36   = ~Ah, I'm not so confident with enchanting wood in such... mundane shape. Maybe Garalt or Matha could help you with this? That would be the tower armorer or fletcher. I am sure I can sell you the needed magics for it, though, if you want to have a look.~
@37   = ~Magic items? You mean like potions and scrolls and stuff?~
@38   = ~Very well.~
@39   = ~Actually, I do. I am working on fortifying the Seatower's magical defenses. For this I need some ingredients normally not available in any shop: one flower of the belladonna plant, an ankheg shell, and the pelt of a winter wolf. If you happen to get hold of one or all of those things then bring them to me and I will pay you accordingly.~
@40   = ~Oh, it is said that they tend to form inside shells found in calm pools of salty water, which are rather rare. Perhaps you will get lucky looking in a secluded tide pool—but I wouldn't know where to look for one along the coast. All the nearby ones have already been picked over. I wouldn't be asking every adventurer who shows up on my doorstep if I knew where to find them, and they usually do not come in greater numbers than one.~
@41   = ~A black pearl! You are the first to actually return with one. And it was... it was right under this tower?! Now I feel foolish. All this time it was right behind a wall... Thank you for bringing it to me. Here is 2,000 gold as compensation.~
@42   = ~Wonderful! I sense you had to go far for that one.~
@43   = ~Yes, yes. I had to go really, *really* far and overcome the most dangerous of situations to get it. It was guarded by a dragon, I tell you. A dragon!~
@44   = ~Actually, I found it right in this kitchen's storeroom.~
@45   = ~Whatever. I'm here now.~
@46   = ~Here is your payment, 300 gold.~
@47   = ~A dragon? Surely you jest!~
@48   = ~The kit... Well, *I* will not go there and give it back. And I really do have a good use for it. Ahem. This will be our little secret, yes?~
@49   = ~Great! And such a fluffy one. I'll give you 600 gold for it.~
@50   = ~Indeed! I hope it didn't put up too much of a fight. Here is 500 gold for your efforts.~
@51   = ~Oh, yes, that always comes in handy. I'll give you 500 gold for it.~
@52   = ~This will be the last I am buying. I do not need it regularly.~
@53   = ~That's weird. I could have sworn I already bought one from you, but I can't seem to find it anywhere... Still, this will be the last one I'll buy from you.~
@54   = ~Sounds like a good deal.~
@55   = ~No, I'll keep it then.~
@56   = ~Here you are.~
@57   = ~I do, actually. I would sell it to you for 500 gold.~
@58   = ~Seems I don't have enough gold.~
@59   = ~No, maybe I'll find another one elsewhere.~
@60   = ~I do, actually! Those half-open flasks are rather hard to come by. Here, a little gold as compensation.~
@61   = ~Ah, no, this one is already too dry.~
@62   = ~I want a fresh one for a special drying process I invented. It should make the pearl even more powerful.~
